quant-2 fix A (docs/research/deepinfer/quant-heads.md): make the negative-scale
fold of patches/marlin-int8-negative-scales.patch lossless, behind
VLLM_MARLIN_INT8_LOSSLESS_FOLD=1 (default off = the existing fold, unchanged).

The W4A8-INT8 Marlin kernel reads group scales as unsigned, so the fold maps a
negative group (s, code v) to (-s, 16 - v clamped to 15): code 0 (q = -8)
becomes 15 and loses one LSB. On the AutoRound body 50.4% of groups are negative
and all of them use code 0 (gpu-results/quant-2-check.md). With the knob on, a
layer with any negative group instead loads as a uint4 zero-point layer on the
kS8 x kU4 kernel that patches/marlin-int8-asym-zp.patch admits: positive groups
keep their codes with zp 8, negative groups get code' = 15 - v, zp 7, |s|.
(code' - zp) * |s| == (v - 8) * s for all 16 codes, so the dequant is
bit-exact. Layers without negative scales stay on the uint4b8 kernel.

Adds VLLM_MARLIN_INT8_LOSSLESS_FOLD to envs.py (hashed into the torch.compile
cache key: it changes the traced weight-type id). Needs the image's
marlin-int8-negative-scales and marlin-int8-asym-zp patches (applied in the
published image). Test: bench/test_marlin_int8_fold.py.

Apply: patch -p1 --forward --fuzz 0 -d /app/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm < quant2-lossless-fold.patch

